.Dd February 27, 2026
.Dt LS 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm ls
.Nd list directory contents
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Ar OPTION ...
.Op Ar FILE ...
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Nm
utility lists information about files and directories.
When no
.Ar FILE
is given,
.Pa .
is listed.
.Pp
Default output is multi-column when writing to a terminal and one entry per line otherwise.
.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl a , -all
Include entries whose names begin with a dot.
.It Fl A , -almost-all
Include dotfiles but still omit
.Pa .
and
.Pa .. .
.It Fl d , -directory
List directory operands themselves instead of their contents.
.It Fl I Ar pattern , -ignore Ns = Ns Ar pattern
Hide implied entries matching
.Ar pattern .
.It Fl l
Long format.
.It Fl g
Long format without owner name.
.It Fl o
Long format without group name.
.It Fl n , -numeric-uid-gid
Long format with numeric UID/GID.
.It Fl 1
One entry per line.
.It Fl C
Multi-column format.
.It Fl m
Comma-separated format.
.It Fl x
By-lines multi-column packing.
.It Fl i , -inode
Print inode numbers.
.It Fl s , -size
Print allocated size in blocks.
.It Fl h , -human-readable
Human readable sizes.
.It Fl k , -kibibytes
Use 1024-byte blocks.
.It Fl -block-size Ns = Ns Ar SIZE
Scale printed sizes by
.Ar SIZE .
.It Fl -si
Use powers of 1000 for human-readable sizes.
.It Fl r , -reverse
Reverse sort order.
.It Fl S
Sort by file size, largest first.
.It Fl t
Sort by selected timestamp, newest first.
.It Fl u
Use access time for
.Fl t
and
.Fl l .
.It Fl c
Use status-change time for
.Fl t
and
.Fl l .
.It Fl U
Do not sort.
.It Fl f
Equivalent to enabling
.Fl a
and
.Fl U ,
and disabling color,
.Fl l ,
and
.Fl s .
.It Fl v
Natural version sort.
.It Fl R , -recursive
Recursive depth-first directory traversal.
.It Fl -hide Ns = Ns Ar pattern
Hide implied entries matching
.Ar pattern
during recursive listing.
.It Fl L , -dereference
Follow symlinks for metadata and traversal.
.It Fl H
Follow symlinks for command-line operands only.
.It Fl F , -classify
Append type indicators
.Pq one of */=>@| .
.It Fl p
Append
.Sq /
to directories.
.It Fl -file-type
Like
.Fl F
but without
.Sq *
for executables.
.It Fl w Ar cols , Fl -width Ns = Ns Ar cols
Set display width in columns.
.It Fl -time Ns = Ns Ar word
Select time field:
.Sy atime | access | use | ctime | status | mtime | modification .
.It Fl -time-style Ns = Ns Ar style
Select time format:
.Sy locale | iso | long-iso | full-iso | +FORMAT .
.It Fl q , -hide-control-chars
Render nongraphic bytes as
.Sq ? .
.It Fl -show-control-chars
Disable control-character hiding.
.It Fl N , -literal
Literal names.
.It Fl Q , -quote-name
C-style quoted names.
.It Fl -quoting-style Ns = Ns Ar word
One of
.Sy literal | shell | shell-always | c | escape .
.It Fl -color Ns = Ns Ar when
Color mode:
.Sy never | auto | always .
.It Fl -help
Display help and exit.
.It Fl -version
Display version and exit.
.El
.Sh OUTPUT MODES
The output mode is selected in this order:
.Bl -bullet
.It
.Fl l
(long format)
.It
.Fl m
(comma)
.It
.Fl 1
(single column)
.It
.Fl x
(by-lines columns)
.It
.Fl C
or terminal auto-detection (columns)
.It
fallback single-column
.El
.Pp
Very narrow displays
.Pq less than 20 columns
fall back to one entry per line.
.Sh LONG FORMAT
Each entry contains mode, link count, owner, group, size/device numbers,
timestamp, and name.
.Pp
The mode field includes file type and rwx bits, including setuid/setgid/sticky
state. A trailing
.Sq +
indicates POSIX ACL xattrs and
.Sq @
indicates non-ACL extended attributes when xattr APIs are available.
.Pp
For symlinks shown as symlinks,
.Nm
prints
.Sq " -> target"
(and marks dangling links).
.Pp
Directory long listings print a leading
.Sq total N
line.
.Sh SORTING
Default sorting is name order.
.Pp
When available in host builds,
.Nm
uses locale collation
.Pq Fn strcoll
for name ordering; target builds use bytewise comparison.
.Pp
Size/time/version sorts use name as a deterministic tie-breaker.
.Sh RECURSION
Recursive mode is depth-first.
Directory headers are printed before each subtree.
Permission/open errors are reported and traversal continues.
Directory cycles are detected using
.Pq dev,ino
pairs and reported.
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It 0
Successful completion.
.It 1
Minor problems (for example, unreadable subdirectories).
.It 2
Serious trouble (for example, inaccessible command-line operand, allocation failure).
.El
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
.Bl -tag -width LS_COLORS
.It Ev LS_COLORS
File-type color map.
.It Ev COLUMNS
Fallback terminal width when ioctl width is unavailable.
.El
.Sh EXAMPLES
List all files including dotfiles:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ ls -a
.Ed
.Pp
Long format sorted by newest modification time:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ ls -lt
.Ed
.Pp
Recursive listing with color forced:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ ls -R --color=always
.Ed
.Sh NOTES
Developer notes:
.Bl -bullet
.It
Column width is computed from rendered entry text width; color escapes are excluded from width math.
.It
Unicode width handling is conservative and degrades safely on non-Unicode libc targets.
.It
ACL/xattr indicators are best-effort and gracefully degrade when xattr APIs are unavailable.
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr stat 2 ,
.Xr readlink 2 ,
.Xr lstat 2
